<%- include('partials/head') %>
<body class="ph-body">
  <%- include('partials/nav') %>

  <section class="ph-page-hero">
    <div class="ph-container">
      <div class="ph-eyebrow">Feature deep-dive</div>
      <h1 class="ph-page-title">Discover everything. Subscribe to anything.</h1>
      <p class="ph-page-lede">iTunes search, Apple's Top Podcasts and seventeen genre charts, manual RSS, OPML in / out, and a share extension that subscribes from Safari.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ph-section">
    <div class="ph-container ph-feature">
      <div class="ph-feature-copy">
        <h2>Top Podcasts, plus seventeen genres.</h2>
        <p>The Search tab opens directly into Apple's <strong>Top Podcasts</strong> chart. Tap a category chip to switch to Arts, Business, Comedy, Education, Government, Health, History, Kids &amp; Family, Leisure, Music, News, Science, Society &amp; Culture, Sports, Technology, True Crime, or TV &amp; Film.</p>
        <p>Pull-to-refresh to fetch the latest. Toggle grid or list view. Tap any cover to see episodes.</p>
      </div>
      <figure class="ph-feature-shot">
        <div class="ph-phone">
          <div class="ph-phone-screen">
            <img src="/public/images/podhaven/search-trending.png" alt="Top Podcasts grid with category chips: Top Podcasts, Arts, Business, and a 4-column grid of trending shows." loading="lazy">
          </div>
        </div>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ph-section ph-section-alt">
    <div class="ph-container ph-feature ph-feature-flip">
      <div class="ph-feature-copy">
        <h2>The whole iTunes catalog, searchable.</h2>
        <p>Search by name, host, keyword, or topic. Results show podcast artwork, episode count, and your subscription status at a glance.</p>
        <p>Independent shows that aren't in the chart? <strong>Manual RSS entry</strong> takes any feed URL. PodHaven parses it the moment you paste.</p>
      </div>
      <figure class="ph-feature-shot">
        <div class="ph-phone">
          <div class="ph-phone-screen">
            <img src="/public/images/podhaven/library-grid.png" alt="The Subscribed library grid showing twelve subscribed podcast covers in a three-column layout." loading="lazy">
          </div>
        </div>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ph-section">
    <div class="ph-container">
      <h2 class="ph-section-title">Bring your library. Take it with you.</h2>
      <div class="ph-grid">
        <div class="ph-card">
          <h3>OPML import</h3>
          <p>Coming from Overcast, Pocket Casts, or Apple Podcasts? Export your subscriptions as OPML, then import into PodHaven in <em>Settings → Importing / Exporting → OPML</em>. The whole library lands subscribed in seconds.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ph-card">
          <h3>OPML export</h3>
          <p>Take your subscriptions wherever you want. PodHaven exports a standards-compliant OPML you can hand to any other app. No lock-in.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ph-card">
          <h3>Share extension</h3>
          <p>Find a podcast in Safari, Mail, or any app. Hit the system share sheet and pick PodHaven — the show lands in your library.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ph-card">
          <h3>Share-by-link</h3>
          <p>Send a podcast or episode to a friend. They get a clean web page (this site) with a one-tap "Open in PodHaven" link.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ph-section ph-section-alt">
    <div class="ph-container">
      <h2 class="ph-section-title">Tags: organize however you actually think.</h2>
      <p class="ph-lede">PodHaven lets you create custom tags and assign them to podcasts. "Tech," "Comedy," "Long Drive," "Sleep" — whatever makes sense to you.</p>
      <ul class="ph-checklist ph-checklist-wide">
        <li>Tag manager in <em>Settings → Organization → Tags</em>, with podcast counts beside each tag.</li>
        <li>Filter the Podcasts library by tag.</li>
        <li>An <em>Untagged</em> bucket helps you tidy up.</li>
        <li>Tags are local — no syncing required, no account to make.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%- include('partials/footer') %>
